PAGES=[
{'slug':'services','crumb':'Services','title':'Water Damage and Mold Services in Marina Del Rey, CA','meta':'Browse water damage services in Marina Del Rey, CA by cause, place, material and storm. Burst pipes, leaks, sewage, drying and mold. Call (424) 550-5662.','h1':'Water Damage and Mold Services in Marina Del Rey, CA','hero_sub':'Twenty service pages, each answering a different question, so you can find the one that matches the problem in front of you or call the 24/7 line and we will sort it out.',
'body':[
{'t':'h2','text':'Pick the service by the question you are asking'},
{'t':'p','text':'People rarely start by searching for the trade name. They search for the symptom: a wet carpet, a stained wall, water standing in a garage, a musty closet. Each page below owns one stage of the job or one cause, and a single loss often moves through several of them in order.'},
{'t':'p','text':'If water is still arriving or standing, start with [emergency water removal](/emergency-water-removal/). If the water has stopped and the building needs to be dried before damage spreads, you want [water mitigation](/water-mitigation/). Our crews work to the published ANSI/IICRC S500 standard for water damage and S520 for mold, and you can ask any company whether it does the same.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'The six core stages'},
{'t':'table','head':['Service','The question it answers','When to call'],'rows':[
 ['[Emergency Water Removal](/emergency-water-removal/)','How do I get standing water out right now?','Active leaks, overflowing fixtures, pooled water'],
 ['[Water Mitigation](/water-mitigation/)','How do I stop the damage from spreading in the next 72 hours?','Water has stopped but walls, floors and ceilings are wet'],
 ['[Water Damage Cleanup](/water-damage-cleanup/)','How do I clean up and sanitize after the water?','Wet debris, contaminated materials, odors'],
 ['[Flood Damage Restoration](/flood-damage-restoration/)','What do I do when water came from outside?','Storm water, groundwater, garages and ground-floor units'],
 ['[Water Damage Repair](/water-damage-repair/)','How do I rebuild once everything is dry?','Drywall, insulation, flooring, paint and cabinets need replacing'],
 ['[Mold Remediation](/mold-remediation/)','What do I do about mold after a leak?','Visible growth, a musty smell or a past leak that was never dried']]},
{'t':'h2','text':'Find your page by cause'},
{'t':'p','text':'When you know what failed, start with the page that covers that failure. Each one explains how the problem shows up in Marina Del Rey buildings, what to shut off first and what the drying plan looks like.'},
{'t':'ul','items':['[Burst pipe water damage](/burst-pipe-water-damage/) for supply lines that fail inside walls and ceilings','[Roof leak water damage](/roof-leak-water-damage/) for rain that gets in from above','[Water heater leak cleanup](/water-heater-leak-cleanup/) for tank and fitting failures','[Appliance leak water damage](/appliance-leak-water-damage/) for washers, dishwashers and refrigerator lines','[AC leak water damage repair](/ac-leak-water-damage/) for condensate lines and wall units','[Slab leak water damage](/slab-leak-water-damage/) for pipes under or inside concrete floors','[Sewage backup cleanup](/sewage-backup-cleanup/) for contaminated water from drains']},
{'t':'h2','text':'Find your page by place or material'},
{'t':'p','text':'Sometimes the room or the surface is the clearer clue. A swollen cabinet base points to the kitchen page, a squishy floor to the carpet page, and a bubbling wall to the drywall page.'},
{'t':'ul','items':['[Kitchen water damage](/kitchen-water-damage/) for sinks, cabinets and appliance corners','[Crawl space water damage](/crawl-space-water-damage/) for raised floors, which are rare around the harbor but real in older buildings','[Commercial water damage](/commercial-water-damage/) for shared and business spaces','[Carpet water damage](/carpet-water-damage/) for wet carpet and padding','[Wall and drywall water damage repair](/drywall-water-damage-repair/) for stained, soft or bubbled walls']},
{'t':'h2','text':'Find your page by storm or structure'},
{'t':'p','text':'Two pages cover the big picture instead of one failure. [Storm water damage](/storm-water-damage/) is for heavy rain and runoff reaching a building, and [structural drying and dehumidification](/structural-drying/) explains the equipment and monitoring that dry framing, subfloors and concrete after any of the causes above.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'How the services connect on a real job'},
{'t':'p','text':'A burst supply line under a bathroom sink is a good example. The first hour is water removal and shut-off. The next two to three days are mitigation, with air movers and dehumidifiers running while crews log moisture readings. Cleanup removes wet cabinet bases and baseboards, repair puts the room back together, and mold work enters only if drying started late or a wall cavity stayed damp.'},
{'t':'p','text':'Not every job needs every stage. A small appliance leak caught within hours may stop at mitigation and a short repair. A storm that pushes water into a ground-floor garage may start at [flood damage restoration](/flood-damage-restoration/) and never involve a ceiling at all.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'What we do not do'},
{'t':'p','text':'We do not handle fire and smoke damage, and we do not provide basement waterproofing, roofing, plumbing or foundation work. Restoration repairs what water already damaged. If a leak keeps coming back, a plumber, roofer or waterproofing contractor has to fix the cause, and we will tell you plainly when that is the case.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'How pricing and scope work'},
{'t':'p','text':'Every job is scoped after the damage is measured. The water category, the wet square footage, the materials involved, the days of drying equipment and the amount of rebuild all move the price, which is why we explain the scope and price before work starts. Want your real number? Call the 24/7 line and describe what you see.'},
{'t':'cta','text':'Not sure which service fits? Describe what you see and the dispatcher will sort it out.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'Where these services are available'},
{'t':'p','text':'Every service is available across Marina Del Rey and the nearby towns of [Venice](/service-area/venice-ca/), [Playa Vista](/service-area/playa-vista-ca/), [Playa del Rey](/service-area/playa-del-rey-ca/), [Culver City](/service-area/culver-city-ca/) and [Santa Monica](/service-area/santa-monica-ca/). Each town page lists its ZIP codes, water utility and permit authority.'}],
'faqs':[('Which service do I need first after a leak?','If water is still present, start with water removal. If the water has stopped but surfaces are wet, start with mitigation. Call the 24/7 line and we will tell you which stage applies to your situation.'),
('Do all of these services come from one company?','Yes. The services are stages of the same job, so the crew that dries your building can also clean up and rebuild it, which keeps documentation in one place for your insurer or association.'),
('Is mold remediation part of every water damage job?','No. Mold work is needed only when growth is present or drying started too late. Quick, thorough drying is the best way to avoid it, and the [mold remediation](/mold-remediation/) page explains when it becomes necessary.'),
('What if my problem is not listed?','Call the 24/7 line anyway. Many losses fit more than one page, and the dispatcher will match what you describe to the right stage.')],
'sidecard':{'h3':'Not sure which page fits?','copy':'Describe the wet area and where the water came from, and the dispatcher will point you to the right stage.','link':('Emergency water removal','/emergency-water-removal/')}},
{'slug':'service-area','crumb':'Service Areas','title':'Water Damage Service Areas Near Marina Del Rey, CA','meta':'Water damage restoration across Marina Del Rey, Venice, Playa Vista, Playa del Rey, Culver City and Santa Monica, CA. ZIP codes, utilities and 24/7 dispatch.','h1':'Water Damage Restoration Service Areas Near Marina Del Rey, CA','hero_sub':'Our 24/7 dispatch covers Marina Del Rey and five nearby towns, each with its own housing, water utility and building department.',
'body':[
{'t':'h2','text':'Marina Del Rey and the towns around it'},
{'t':'p','text':'Marina Del Rey is an unincorporated community of Los Angeles County, ZIP 90292, surrounded by the City of Los Angeles. Water damage does not respect those lines, but permits, utilities and building departments do, so each nearby town has its own page with the details that matter for a repair there.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'The five nearby towns we serve'},
{'t':'p','text':'[Venice](/service-area/venice-ca/), ZIPs 90291 and 90292, sits just northwest of the harbor. Its older bungalows, walk streets and canal-area homes are low-lying, and water damage there often involves aging pipes and wood floors. The page covers LADWP, LADBS and the ZIPs we cover.'},
{'t':'p','text':'[Playa Vista](/service-area/playa-vista-ca/), ZIP 90094, is a newer community built on the former Hughes Aircraft site beginning in the early 2000s, so supply lines, appliances and shared systems matter more than old plumbing. [Playa del Rey](/service-area/playa-del-rey-ca/), ZIP 90293, lies south of the harbor between the beach, the lagoons and the bluffs, with a coastal setting that shapes its moisture problems.'},
{'t':'p','text':'[Culver City](/service-area/culver-city-ca/), ZIPs 90230 and 90232, is its own incorporated city with its own Building Safety Division, and Ballona Creek runs through it. [Santa Monica](/service-area/santa-monica-ca/), ZIPs 90401 through 90405, is also its own city with its own water division and permit center, and most of its homes are rented, which changes who has to be told about a leak.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'Neighborhood pages'},
{'t':'p','text':'Three smaller places have their own pages because their water, tide and permit questions differ. The [Venice Canals](/service-area/venice-canals-ca/) sit on low ground behind tide gates, the [Marina Peninsula](/service-area/marina-peninsula-ca/) lies between the harbor and the beach, and the [Oxford Triangle](/service-area/oxford-triangle-ca/) sits next to the Oxford Basin flood control facility.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'Nearby places we mention but do not build pages for'},
{'t':'p','text':'Calls also come in from Westchester and from El Segundo near the south end of the coast, and from the Del Rey and Palms neighborhoods of Los Angeles near Culver City. If your address is in one of them, call the line and we will confirm coverage for your block.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'ZIP codes we serve'},
{'t':'ul','items':['Marina Del Rey: 90292','Venice: 90291 and 90292','Playa Vista: 90094','Playa del Rey: 90293','Culver City: 90230 and 90232','Santa Monica: 90401, 90402, 90403, 90404 and 90405']},
{'t':'p','text':'A ZIP code is a convenient way to describe coverage, but the street address is what matters when a crew is dispatched. Tell the dispatcher your building, floor and nearest cross street, and mention whether you have to coordinate with property management or an association.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'Jurisdictions at a glance'},
{'t':'table','head':['Place','Governing body','Typical permit contact'],'rows':[
 ['Marina Del Rey','Unincorporated Los Angeles County, marina managed by the county Department of Beaches and Harbors','County Public Works Building and Safety, confirm for your parcel'],
 ['Venice, Playa Vista, Playa del Rey','City of Los Angeles','LADBS'],
 ['Culver City','City of Culver City','Culver City Building Safety Division at City Hall'],
 ['Santa Monica','City of Santa Monica','Santa Monica Permit Services Center']]},
{'t':'p','text':'Permit rules vary, so ask the building department for your address before a rebuild. We can tell you what work usually needs inspection, but the department decides.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'Why the town matters to the repair'},
{'t':'p','text':'Water extraction and drying look the same in every town, but the paperwork around the rebuild does not. A drywall and flooring repair in Culver City may involve the Building Safety Division, while the same repair in Venice falls to LADBS, and a Marina Del Rey address in the unincorporated county answers to County Public Works. Confirm which body covers your parcel before ordering materials.'},
{'t':'p','text':'Utilities differ too. The county runs a small Marina del Rey water system for the harbor leaseholds, the City of Santa Monica runs its own water division, and many Culver City addresses are served by Golden State Water Company. Your water bill shows who serves your address, and that is who to call about a main line or a meter.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'If you manage more than one building'},
{'t':'p','text':'Property managers and associations often call about several addresses at once, for example after a storm. Give the dispatcher each building, the affected floors and any access rules. We document each address separately so each claim and each association file stays clean, and we explain the scope and price per building before work starts.'},
{'t':'cta','text':'Not sure whether your address is covered? Call the 24/7 line with the street and cross street.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'Not sure which page fits you?'},
{'t':'p','text':'Start from the problem rather than the place if that is easier. [Emergency water removal](/emergency-water-removal/) covers standing water anywhere we serve, and [flood damage restoration](/flood-damage-restoration/) covers storm and drain water in low-lying addresses throughout the area.'}],
'faqs':[('Do you serve addresses outside the towns listed?','Often yes. Call the 24/7 line with your address and we will confirm whether a crew can be dispatched there.'),('Is dispatch the same in every town?','Dispatch runs around the clock everywhere we serve, and response is same-day when available. We do not promise a fixed arrival time because traffic and conditions change.')]},

{'slug':'about','crumb':'About','title':'About Marina Del Rey, CA Water Damage Pros | 24/7 Service','meta':'Learn how Marina Del Rey Water Damage Pros handles water damage restoration and mold remediation, what we follow and what we do not do. Call 24/7.','h1':'About Marina Del Rey Water Damage Pros','hero_sub':'A 24/7 water damage restoration and mold remediation service for Marina Del Rey and the nearby towns of Venice, Playa Vista, Playa del Rey, Culver City and Santa Monica.',
'body':[
{'t':'h2','text':'What we do'},
{'t':'p','text':'Marina Del Rey Water Damage Pros answers the phone when water is where it should not be. We dispatch licensed and insured restoration professionals to extract water, dry structures, clean and sanitize, rebuild damaged materials and assess mold that follows a leak. The office address is 4025 Lincoln Blvd in Marina del Rey, and the dispatch line is answered by a person at every hour, because a recorded message does not stop a leak.'},
{'t':'p','text':'Our focus is residential and multi-unit buildings around the harbor and the Westside, where condominiums, apartments, older bungalows and newer townhomes each fail in different ways. A supply line failure in a condominium and a storm drain backup in a garage are different jobs, and we treat them that way.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'The standards we work to'},
{'t':'p','text':'Water damage work in the United States follows two published standards from the Institute of Inspection, Cleaning and Restoration Certification. ANSI/IICRC S500 covers professional water damage restoration, including water categories and drying goals. ANSI/IICRC S520 covers professional mold remediation. We describe our process in those terms, and we encourage you to ask any company, including us, whether its crews work to them.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'How a job runs'},
{'t':'p','text':'The first call is a conversation, not a form. You describe the damage and we tell you what to shut off, what to photograph and what to leave alone. A crew assesses with moisture meters and thermal imaging, explains the scope and how the price is set before work starts, and then begins extraction and drying. Moisture readings are logged on each visit so the dry-out is measured, not assumed.'},
{'t':'p','text':'Afterward you have photos, readings and a written scope. Those help your insurer, your landlord or your homeowners association understand what happened and what was done, though we never promise what an insurer will approve.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'The buildings we see most'},
{'t':'p','text':'Around the harbor, most calls come from multi-story condominium and apartment buildings with shared walls, floors and risers. A leak in one unit travels, so a call about a stained ceiling is often a call about the unit above, and sometimes about the one above that. We ask who owns the plumbing, who manages access and which units sit below, because those answers decide how fast a crew can reach the source.'},
{'t':'p','text':'Toward Venice and Santa Monica the mix shifts to older bungalows and small multifamily buildings, and toward Playa Vista it shifts to newer townhomes and mid-rise buildings. The [service area page](/service-area/) explains how each town differs, and [water damage repair](/water-damage-repair/) covers what happens when the rebuild begins.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'What to expect on the day'},
{'t':'p','text':'A crew arrives with moisture meters, a thermal imaging camera, extraction units, air movers and LGR dehumidifiers. The first hour is spent finding where the water went, not only where it shows. Wet materials that cannot be dried come out, the drying equipment goes in and you receive a plain explanation of what each machine is doing and when it will be checked.'},
{'t':'p','text':'We tell you when the drying is finished by showing the readings, not by guessing. If the damage turns out larger than the first look suggested, we explain the change before continuing, and you decide how to proceed.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'What we do not do'},
{'t':'ul','items':['We do not handle fire and smoke damage.','We do not offer basement waterproofing or foundation repair. If water keeps coming in, that is a different trade, and we will say so.','We do not rent drying equipment. Air movers and dehumidifiers run as part of a job.','We do not give health advice about mold. Health questions belong to a physician.']},
{'t':'h2','text':'Where we work'},
{'t':'p','text':'We cover Marina Del Rey and the nearby towns of [Venice](/service-area/venice-ca/), [Playa Vista](/service-area/playa-vista-ca/), [Playa del Rey](/service-area/playa-del-rey-ca/), [Culver City](/service-area/culver-city-ca/) and [Santa Monica](/service-area/santa-monica-ca/). Our [services](/services/) range from emergency extraction to the final repair.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'Contact'},
{'t':'p','text':'Call the 24/7 line any time, or visit the [contact page](/contact/) for the address and email. We prefer the phone because water damage is urgent and a conversation gets a crew moving faster than a message does.'}],
'faqs':[('Are your crews licensed and insured?','Yes. We work with licensed and insured restoration professionals. We do not publish license numbers on this site, and you can ask any company to confirm its credentials before work begins.'),('Do you follow industry standards?','Our process follows the published ANSI/IICRC S500 water damage and S520 mold remediation standards. Ask any restoration company whether its crews work to them.')]},

{'slug':'contact','crumb':'Contact','title':'Contact Marina Del Rey, CA Water Damage Pros | Call 24/7','meta':'Call the 24/7 water damage line for Marina Del Rey, CA, or find our address and email. Know what to have ready before you call and how pricing works.','h1':'Contact Marina Del Rey Water Damage Pros','hero_sub':'The fastest way to reach a crew is the 24/7 phone line. Here is the address, the email and what to have ready when you call.',
'body':[
{'t':'h2','text':'Call, do not wait'},
{'t':'p','text':'Water damage gets more expensive every hour it sits. Call the line, tell the dispatcher what you see and answer a few questions about the building and the source. We will tell you what to shut off while the crew is arranged. Calls to our line may be recorded for quality and training purposes.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'Have these ready'},
{'t':'ul','items':['Your address, building name if any, and floor or unit number.','Where the water came from and whether it has stopped.','Roughly how much is wet and what materials are involved, such as carpet, wood floor, drywall or cabinets.','Whether an association or property manager must approve access.','Photos or video if you can take them safely.']},
{'t':'h2','text':'How scope and price are set'},
{'t':'p','text':'We explain the scope and price before work starts. The water category, the wet area, the materials, the days of drying and the amount of rebuild decide the number, so a quote over the phone would only be a guess. After the damage is measured, you decide whether to proceed.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'Where we are'},
{'t':'p','text':'Our address is 4025 Lincoln Blvd, Marina del Rey, CA 90292, and our crews dispatch from there around the clock to [Marina Del Rey](/service-area/), [Venice](/service-area/venice-ca/), [Playa Vista](/service-area/playa-vista-ca/), [Playa del Rey](/service-area/playa-del-rey-ca/), [Culver City](/service-area/culver-city-ca/) and [Santa Monica](/service-area/santa-monica-ca/). Our [services](/services/) page lists everything we handle.'}],
'faqs':[('Can I request service by email?','Email works for non-urgent questions, but any active leak should go to the phone line so a crew can be arranged immediately.'),('What are your hours?','The dispatch line is open 24 hours a day, every day, including holidays.')]},

{'slug':'blog','crumb':'Blog','title':'Water Damage and Mold Guides for Marina Del Rey, CA','meta':'Homeowner guides on ceiling leaks, wood floors, insurance, mold and drying for Marina Del Rey, CA, written around local buildings, utilities and storms.','h1':'Water Damage and Mold Guides for Marina Del Rey, CA','hero_sub':'Plain-language guides on leaks, drying, mold and insurance, each tied to how buildings and weather around Marina Del Rey actually behave.','intro':'Each guide answers a question people ask after a leak or a storm, and each closes with a local note on utilities, permits or geography. If water is spreading right now, skip the reading and call the 24/7 line.','body':[]},

{'slug':'privacy','crumb':'Privacy Policy','title':'Privacy Policy | Marina Del Rey Water Damage Pros','meta':'How Marina Del Rey Water Damage Pros handles information from phone calls and website visits. Call-only service with no forms. Calls may be recorded.','h1':'Privacy Policy','hero_sub':'This site is call-only. It has no forms, and this policy explains what information a phone call or a visit can involve.','badge':'<span class="badge">Policy</span>',
'body':[
{'t':'h2','text':'Information we receive'},
{'t':'p','text':'When you call our line, we receive your phone number and whatever you tell us, such as your address, a description of the damage and details about your building. We use that information to dispatch a crew, explain scope and price, and follow up on the job.'},
{'t':'p','text':'Calls to our line may be recorded for quality and training purposes. If you do not want a call recorded, tell the dispatcher at the start of the call.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'This website'},
{'t':'p','text':'This website does not contain forms and does not ask you to type personal information into a page. Pages load fonts from Google Fonts, and some pages embed a Google Maps view. Those services may receive your browser address and standard request details under their own privacy policies.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'How we use information'},
{'t':'p','text':'We use call information to provide the service you asked for, to document the job, to improve how our dispatchers answer calls and to meet legal and insurance documentation needs. We share job details with the crew assigned to your address and with parties you ask us to coordinate with, such as an adjuster or property manager.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'Retention and your choices'},
{'t':'p','text':'We keep job and call records for as long as needed to support the work and any related claim. You can ask us to correct information you gave us or to tell you what we hold by calling the line or emailing contact@marinadelreywaterdamagepros.com.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'Children'},
{'t':'p','text':'Our service is intended for property owners, tenants and managers, not for children, and we do not knowingly collect information from children.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'Changes to this policy'},
{'t':'p','text':'We may update this policy as the site or service changes. The date below shows when it was last changed. Questions go to the email above or to the 24/7 line, and our [contact page](/contact/) has the address.'},
{'t':'p','text':'Last updated: 2026.'}]},

{'slug':'terms','crumb':'Terms of Service','title':'Terms of Service | Marina Del Rey Water Damage Pros','meta':'Terms for using the Marina Del Rey Water Damage Pros website and phone line, including how scope and price are set and the limits of general information.','h1':'Terms of Service','hero_sub':'These terms cover the use of this website and the phone line. Work on a specific job is covered by the scope and price we explain before it starts.','badge':'<span class="badge">Terms</span>',
'body':[
{'t':'h2','text':'Using this website'},
{'t':'p','text':'The information on this site is general. It describes how water damage restoration and mold remediation usually work and is not advice about your specific building, policy or health. Conditions differ, and only an on-site assessment can tell what a particular loss needs.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'Phone calls'},
{'t':'p','text':'Calls to our line may be recorded for quality and training purposes. By calling, you understand this and agree that we may use the call to dispatch a crew and document the job.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'Scope, price and authorization'},
{'t':'p','text':'We explain the scope and price before work starts. Work begins only after you or an authorized representative agree to it. If conditions change during a job, such as hidden damage found behind a wall, we explain the change before continuing.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'No guarantees about insurance or timing'},
{'t':'p','text':'We document damage to support an insurance claim, but we do not decide coverage and we do not promise what an insurer will approve. We offer same-day response when available and do not guarantee a specific arrival time.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'Service area'},
{'t':'p','text':'Coverage is described on our [service area page](/service-area/). We may decline work outside it or work that is outside our services, such as fire damage or waterproofing.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'Limitation of liability'},
{'t':'p','text':'To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses arising from use of this website. Nothing here limits rights you have under California law or limits liability that cannot be limited by law.'},
{'t':'h2','text':'Contact'},
{'t':'p','text':'Questions about these terms can be sent to contact@marinadelreywaterdamagepros.com or to our address at 4025 Lincoln Blvd, Marina del Rey, CA 90292. Last updated: 2026.'}]},
]
